From ee96069cf2a3be7e615cfdf2690363c664580387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:37:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): cut sweep_shared_blockers and
 restore_missing_checks reclaim cost (G2e) [daveey]

Follow-up of G2 (t_bc85e06710e0e9ab): P1 at e5d8621dd7a2 read reclaim 0.490% vs the 0.4% budget; sweep_shared_blockers
3.00 ms/run and dispatcher_drain 2.02 ms/run were the largest movers.

- BlockerState.__deepcopy__: blocker inputs copy ~100 states per store/hit; only the two int maps need copying.
- kanban_blocker_rows: hand out the held task mapping as is while nothing changed and keep the run-id-sorted assertion
  rows per held mapping (sorted once per change, not once per ask; the lookback window is still applied per ask).
- kanban_wake_check.restore_missing_checks: one batched MAX(id) read names each card's newest park; a card whose newest
  park is already settled (_RESTORE_SEEN, including parks overtaken by a later claimed/spawned) is skipped without
  per-card reads. A newer park reopens it. Semantics unchanged: no sweep gating, expired-claim reclaim, crash detection
  and quota recovery untouched.
- scripts/kanban_reclaim_replay_bench.py: --hub-sync SHADOW plants the hub's sync-shadow replica; BENCH_CALLERS/CALLEES.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_g2e_reclaim_cost.py 7 tests; with the three source files reverted 4 fail (RED), 3 pass
(guards); GREEN with the change. 98 test files importing the touched modules: 1999 passed. scripts/check: ok.
Replay (synthetic board, churn 4): sweep_shared_blockers 3.481 -> 3.014 ms/tick, whole tick 84.7 -> 81.3 ms.
The P1 readback on the deployed head follows.
